{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Upon the earth.</b> To exclude those that are on it." "<b>The ḥoled.</b> belette (Old French), i.e., mole (mouschetil in Old French). The mouse — rat (Old French) in לע״ז." "<b>The tzav.</b> pourvuial (Old French)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "Chizkuni cites Old French glosses in transliteration: ביליט״א = belette (weasel), מושטי״יל possibly mouschetil (a type of mole or shrew), רט״ו = rat. לע״ז = la'az, the vernacular (Old French).", 2 "Old French gloss פרווייט״א, likely identifying the tzav as a type of toad or frog."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:26.189834431Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}